From 48d1f1cee870af69aa368b751757edec8dce6d16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:03:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat(control-plane): authenticate API keys bound to
 tenants

The API took the tenant from the X-Tenant-Id header, so any caller that
could reach the control plane could read or write any tenant's resources
by changing one header; the documented "the gateway verifies it" premise
did not hold because nothing stopped direct access.

Resolve every /api/v1 request to a verified Principal instead:

* apikey mode (default): Authorization: Bearer <key>. A JSON key file
  (FORGEMESH_API_KEYS_FILE, SHA-256 digests only, shared with the gateway)
  binds each key to a tenant, subject and read/write scopes. A tenant
  header that disagrees with the key's tenant is rejected with 403 rather
  than silently rewritten.
* dev mode: trust X-Tenant-Id as before; main() refuses to start it on a
  non-loopback address and the app logs a warning.

Missing credentials answer 401 with WWW-Authenticate, insufficient scope
403, and an app without an injected authenticator fails closed with 503.
Startup fails when apikey mode has no readable key file. Add
"python -m forgemesh.controlplane.auth keygen" to mint keys.
